WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.630 --> 00:00:03.090
- [Host] This little
e-cigarette made Juul Labs

00:00:03.090 --> 00:00:07.020
one of the most valuable startups
in Silicon Valley in 2018.

00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:11.730
At its peak, the company
was worth $38 billion,

00:00:11.730 --> 00:00:16.730
Juul's popularity swelled
as US cigarette sales fell.

00:00:16.980 --> 00:00:19.590
It even spawned a verb, Juuling.

00:00:19.590 --> 00:00:22.770
- And it upended the
entire tobacco industry,

00:00:22.770 --> 00:00:25.470
today, its future is in doubt.

00:00:25.470 --> 00:00:27.930
- [Host] Juul has narrowly
escaped bankruptcy,

00:00:27.930 --> 00:00:30.840
laid off nearly three
quarters of its workers,

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:35.223
and one of its largest shareholders
divested its 35% stake.

00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:39.480
Now it's in limbo waiting
to see if it can continue

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:41.370
selling its products.

00:00:41.370 --> 00:00:43.018
So what went wrong?

00:00:43.018 --> 00:00:44.370
(upbeat music)

00:00:44.370 --> 00:00:47.790
The first Juul vaporizer
was released in 2015,

00:00:47.790 --> 00:00:51.780
its stated mission eliminate
traditional cigarettes,

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:54.030
some early reviews were positive.

00:00:54.030 --> 00:00:54.960
- [Narrator] The Juul from PAX

00:00:54.960 --> 00:00:57.660
might be the best designed
e-cigarette out there.

00:00:57.660 --> 00:01:00.060
- [Host] Following its
release e-cigarette use jumped

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:04.320
among teens while use of other
tobacco products declined,

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:06.480
thanks largely to the popularity of Juul.

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:07.920
- It had this cool sort

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:12.160
of sleek device that
looked like a USB charger.

00:01:12.160 --> 00:01:15.500
It was unlike anything
that had come before it.

00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:18.499
It was sort of like the
Apple of e-cigarettes.

00:01:18.499 --> 00:01:20.760
- [Host] Juul's early ad campaign

00:01:20.760 --> 00:01:24.350
in 2015 featured young
people puffing and partying

00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:29.190
and flavors like mint and
mango appeal to younger users.

00:01:29.190 --> 00:01:32.280
- I've never been exposed to
tobacco, why would I try it?

00:01:32.280 --> 00:01:34.380
But since I was exposed to fruit obviously

00:01:34.380 --> 00:01:37.713
and mango and mint that I
just thought it was okay.

00:01:37.713 --> 00:01:40.920
- [Host] Juul was the
e-cigarette brand of choice.

00:01:40.920 --> 00:01:44.970
- In 2018, Juul was dominating
the e-cigarette market,

00:01:44.970 --> 00:01:46.710
its sales were soaring

00:01:46.710 --> 00:01:50.580
and it was the number
one e-cigarette brand.

00:01:50.580 --> 00:01:51.960
- [Host] But in April of that year,

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:55.470
the FDA started taking a closer
look at the products appeal

00:01:55.470 --> 00:01:59.940
to teens facing that probe
and mounting criticism,

00:01:59.940 --> 00:02:03.060
Juul said it would stop
selling flavored refill pods

00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:05.520
in an effort to stem underage use.

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:07.980
- As a mom of teenagers,
it is certainly a step

00:02:07.980 --> 00:02:08.813
in the right direction.

00:02:08.813 --> 00:02:09.840
- It's the least they could do.

00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:12.540
- [Host] Then in December,
despite these concerns,

00:02:12.540 --> 00:02:15.750
the biggest tobacco
company in the US, Altria,

00:02:15.750 --> 00:02:18.930
the parent company of Philip Morris USA,

00:02:18.930 --> 00:02:22.290
took a 35% stake in the startup.

00:02:22.290 --> 00:02:25.080
Altria saw smokers switching to vaping

00:02:25.080 --> 00:02:30.000
and its own e-cigarettes
couldn't match Juul's popularity.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.972
It paid 12.8 billion for its stake,

00:02:32.972 --> 00:02:36.363
valuing Juul at $38 billion.

00:02:37.230 --> 00:02:40.260
But the deal only increased
regulatory scrutiny

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:41.550
on the company.

00:02:41.550 --> 00:02:45.630
- We are in the midst of
a youth vaping epidemic.

00:02:45.630 --> 00:02:48.401
- Regulators started looking
at Altria's investment

00:02:48.401 --> 00:02:51.715
and the FDA, the Federal Trade Commission

00:02:51.715 --> 00:02:54.390
and Attorneys General
across the country were

00:02:54.390 --> 00:02:58.140
all still investigating
Juul's marketing practices.

00:02:58.140 --> 00:02:59.790
- And so we have a responsibility

00:02:59.790 --> 00:03:01.140
as the Chief Law enforcement officer

00:03:01.140 --> 00:03:03.510
in the state of New York
to protect young people,

00:03:03.510 --> 00:03:06.030
and that's what we are
doing with this litigation.

00:03:06.030 --> 00:03:09.120
- As the US cracked down
on the e-cigarette industry

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:12.360
and Juul voluntarily stopped
most of its marketing,

00:03:12.360 --> 00:03:15.780
Juul sales and market share fell.

00:03:15.780 --> 00:03:20.780
In 2021, Juul reported a
net loss of 259 million

00:03:21.030 --> 00:03:23.130
and an 11% decline in sales,

00:03:23.130 --> 00:03:26.550
according to a disclosure the
company made to employees.

00:03:26.550 --> 00:03:29.619
Juul said it was working to
regain the public's trust.

00:03:29.619 --> 00:03:34.619
Then in June, 2022, the FDA
dealt Juul a major blow.

00:03:35.215 --> 00:03:38.130
- Juul electronic cigarettes
can no longer be sold

00:03:38.130 --> 00:03:39.030
in the US.

00:03:39.030 --> 00:03:41.490
- [Host] The agency ordered
Juul to pull its products

00:03:41.490 --> 00:03:45.900
off of US shelves, but not for
alleged marketing to teens.

00:03:45.900 --> 00:03:47.850
According to FDA documents viewed

00:03:47.850 --> 00:03:49.140
by the Wall Street Journal,

00:03:49.140 --> 00:03:52.200
Juul hadn't sufficiently
answered the agency's questions

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:55.290
about whether Juul's
products might expose users

00:03:55.290 --> 00:03:58.200
to chemicals that could
pose a health risk.

00:03:58.200 --> 00:04:02.550
- Juul immediately appealed
and the FDA issued a stay

00:04:02.550 --> 00:04:03.900
on the order, which means

00:04:03.900 --> 00:04:07.350
that Juul's products were
allowed to remain on the market,

00:04:07.350 --> 00:04:08.550
pending an appeal.

00:04:08.550 --> 00:04:10.890
- [Host] In July, the FDA
said it would allow Juul

00:04:10.890 --> 00:04:13.260
to continue selling products in the US,

00:04:13.260 --> 00:04:14.970
its most important market.

00:04:14.970 --> 00:04:15.803
By this point,

00:04:15.803 --> 00:04:18.660
underage vaping had fallen
and Juul was no longer

00:04:18.660 --> 00:04:21.570
the number one e-cigarette
brand among teens.

00:04:21.570 --> 00:04:23.293
It wasn't even in the top 10,

00:04:24.259 --> 00:04:26.730
Juul was soon facing bankruptcy.

00:04:26.730 --> 00:04:29.850
- It was unclear whether
Juul's products were gonna be

00:04:29.850 --> 00:04:32.640
able to remain on the market
or would have to be pulled off.

00:04:32.640 --> 00:04:36.330
And because its future
was unclear, Juul suddenly

00:04:36.330 --> 00:04:40.740
was unable to take out traditional
loans or get investments

00:04:40.740 --> 00:04:43.740
that would help cover the
cost of its legal liabilities.

00:04:43.740 --> 00:04:44.573
And some

00:04:44.573 --> 00:04:48.810
of these lawsuits were scheduled
to come up soon for trial.

00:04:48.810 --> 00:04:49.643
- [Host] In November,

00:04:49.643 --> 00:04:53.190
Juul said it had secured
financing to avoid bankruptcy.

00:04:53.190 --> 00:04:55.950
Its saviors came in the
form of Hyatt Hotel's heir,

00:04:55.950 --> 00:04:59.790
Nick Pritzker and California
investor Riaz Valani.

00:04:59.790 --> 00:05:03.300
- These two men basically
gave Juul a lifeline.

00:05:03.300 --> 00:05:08.300
They gave Juul a cash infusion
to help Juul stay afloat

00:05:09.600 --> 00:05:13.230
and cover some of these legal settlements.

00:05:13.230 --> 00:05:15.450
- [Host] Juul announced
plans to lay off a third

00:05:15.450 --> 00:05:18.750
of its global staff leaving
the company with a fraction

00:05:18.750 --> 00:05:23.670
of the 3,000 workers it had
in 2019 and a month later,

00:05:23.670 --> 00:05:27.660
Pritzker and Valani helped
Juul make another big step.

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:30.810
The company agreed to pay $1.7 billion

00:05:30.810 --> 00:05:32.820
in a broad legal settlement covering more

00:05:32.820 --> 00:05:36.718
than 5,000 lawsuits
over marketing to teens.

00:05:36.718 --> 00:05:38.820
Juul denied wrongdoing.

00:05:38.820 --> 00:05:41.850
- It really helped clarify Juul's future

00:05:41.850 --> 00:05:44.345
with those lawsuits hanging over it,

00:05:44.345 --> 00:05:47.700
its future had been somewhat in doubt

00:05:47.700 --> 00:05:51.780
and so it was able to resolve the bulk

00:05:51.780 --> 00:05:54.930
of the legal liability that it faced.

00:05:54.930 --> 00:05:57.000
- [Host] Fast forward to March, 2023

00:05:57.000 --> 00:05:59.100
when Altria divested its minority stake

00:05:59.100 --> 00:06:02.970
in Juul at a loss of
at least $12.5 billion.

00:06:02.970 --> 00:06:06.840
- The fact that Altria was a
big shareholder in Juul meant

00:06:06.840 --> 00:06:09.690
that Juul did not have
complete freedom to enter

00:06:09.690 --> 00:06:13.650
into new investment
agreements with other parties.

00:06:13.650 --> 00:06:17.463
Juul is has complete freedom to either,

00:06:17.463 --> 00:06:20.045
come up with distribution agreements,

00:06:20.045 --> 00:06:22.290
new investment agreements

00:06:22.290 --> 00:06:25.560
or sell the company
outright to someone else.

00:06:25.560 --> 00:06:27.012
- [Host] On April 12th,

00:06:27.012 --> 00:06:31.110
Juul agreed to pay $462 million
to settle lawsuits filed

00:06:31.110 --> 00:06:34.020
by six states and the
District of Columbia.

00:06:34.020 --> 00:06:37.740
Five days later, it settled
its last pending lawsuit.

00:06:37.740 --> 00:06:38.970
- The declining health and wellbeing

00:06:38.970 --> 00:06:40.950
of millions of teens and
young adults will not be

00:06:40.950 --> 00:06:44.430
a footnote in Juul's business plans.

00:06:44.430 --> 00:06:47.280
- [Host] Today, Juul's
future is uncertain.

00:06:47.280 --> 00:06:48.896
- The big question remains,

00:06:48.896 --> 00:06:52.513
what is the FDA going to say and decide

00:06:52.513 --> 00:06:55.140
about whether it's products
can remain on the market,

00:06:55.140 --> 00:06:58.320
if its products do have
to come off the market

00:06:58.320 --> 00:07:02.837
it would need a lifeline
of some sort to keep going.

00:07:02.837 --> 00:07:05.337
(soft music)

